  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "",
    "constraints": [
      "ChefCorp has NNN employees. Each employee belongs to **exactly one** of the MMM departments. Each department is headed by **exactly one** of the employees belonging to that department.",
      "The management structure of ChefCorp is as follows:",
      "Each employee of a department (including its head) is in contact with every other employee of that department.",
      "The head of each department is in contact with the heads of all the other departments.",
      "For example, let N=7N = 7N=7, M=3M = 3M=3 and employees 1,2,31, \\textbf{2}, 31,2,3 belong to the first department, employees 4,5\\textbf{4}, 54,5 belong to the second department and employees 6,7\\textbf{6}, 76,7 belong to the third department (employees in bold represent the heads of the departments). The following pairs of employees are in contact with each other: (1,2),(1,3),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7),(2,4),(4,6),(2,6)(1, 2), (1, 3), (2, 3), (4, 5), (6, 7), (2, 4), (4, 6), (2, 6)(1,2),(1,3),(2,3),(4,5),(6,7),(2,4),(4,6),(2,6).",
      "However, due to some inexplicable reasons, ChefCorp loses all its data on the departments. Given the total number of employees NNN and **every pair** of employees who are in contact with each other, can you help recover the number of departments and the employees belonging to each of the departments?",
      "Input Format",
      "The first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.",
      "The first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the total number of employees in ChefCorp.",
      "The second line of each test case contains a single integer KKK — the number of pairs of employees in contact with each other.",
      "KKK lines follow. The ithi^{th}ith of these KKK lines contain two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting that employee uiu_iui​ is in contact with viv_ivi​.",
      "Output Format",
      "For each test case, output the following:",
      "In the first line output MMM — the number of departments.",
      "In the second line, output NNN space-separated integers D1,D2,…,DND_1, D_2, \\ldots, D_ND1​,D2​,…,DN​ (1≤Di≤M)(1 \\leq D_i \\leq M)(1≤Di​≤M) — denoting that the ithi^{th}ith employee belongs to the DithD_i^{th}Dith​ department.",
      "In the third line, output MMM space-separated integers H1,H2,…,HMH_1, H_2, \\ldots, H_MH1​,H2​,…,HM​ (1≤Hi≤N,Hi≠Hj(1 \\leq H_i \\leq N, H_i \\neq H_j(1≤Hi​≤N,Hi​=Hj​ when i≠j)i \\neq j)i=j) — denoting that the HithH_i^{th}Hith​ employee is the head of the ithi^{th}ith department.",
      "If there are multiple answers, **output any**. It is guaranteed that at least one solution always exists.",
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤10002 \\leq N \\leq 10002≤N≤1000",
      "1≤K≤N⋅(N−1)21 \\leq K \\leq \\frac{N\\cdot(N-1)}{2}1≤K≤2N⋅(N−1)​",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "ui≠viu_i \\neq v_iui​=vi​ for each 1≤i≤K1 \\leq i \\leq K1≤i≤K.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 300030003000."
    ],
